meta {
  name: Service Intake (as CSR)
  type: http
  seq: 60
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/assigned/{{reconRowId}}/service-intake
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconSvcCsrToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "primaryContact": {
      "firstName": "Morgan",
      "lastName": "Hale",
      "dateOfBirth": "1979-03-21",
      "phone": "(918) 555-0142",
      "email": "morgan.hale@example.com"
    },
    "address": {
      "street": "4410 S Peoria Ave",
      "city": "Tulsa",
      "state": "OK",
      "zip": "74105"
    },
    "members": [
      { "firstName": "Riley", "lastName": "Hale", "dateOfBirth": "1981-07-02", "role": "Spouse" }
    ],
    "policy": {
      "policyNumber": "900299991",
      "policyType": "Auto",
      "premium": 793.08,
      "itemCount": 1,
      "effectiveDate": "2026-10-15",
      "newBusinessApplication": {
        "key": "{{reconSvcKey}}",
        "filename": "morgan-hale-application.pdf",
        "contentType": "application/pdf",
        "size": 2048
      }
    },
    "assignedCsrId": "{{reconSvcCsrId}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("reconSvcHouseholdId", res.getBody().householdId);
    bru.setVar("reconSvcPolicyId", res.getBody().policyId);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("names what it created, welcome call included", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.householdId).to.be.a("string");
    expect(body.policyId).to.be.a("string");
    expect(body.onboardingId).to.be.a("string");
    expect(body.ticketId).to.be.a("string");
  });

  test("finishes the row: Service intake, done, never a sale", function () {
    const outcome = res.getBody().row.outcome;
    expect(outcome).to.include({
      kind: "service_intake",
      status: "done",
      step: null,
      leadId: null,
      dealId: null,
    });
    expect(outcome.householdId).to.equal(res.getBody().householdId);
    expect(outcome.ticketId).to.equal(res.getBody().ticketId);
    expect(outcome.completedBy.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("reconSvcCsrId"));
    expect(res.getBody().row.review).to.include({
      status: "resolved",
      resolution: "service_intake_recorded",
    });
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /carrier-reconciliation/assigned/:rowId/service-intake — set a 1-800 policy up for service

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation` (enabled for the agency); CRM service
    must be on too — the hand-off opens a welcome call
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:read` **or** `leads:read` (the
    class gate), **and** `leads:write`, checked on every call
  - **Data scope:** the row's assignee only. A pinned `householdId` must be
    inside the caller's client scope.

  PAC-173 PR 5. Allstate sold the policy directly (1-800 / allstate.com) and
  assigned it to the agency, which **services** it: it is never a sale. One
  request records:

  1. **The client**, as a lead's household is captured — the same contact and
     household resolution as `POST /leads` (DOB, phone and email required on
     the primary), the members, and the primary membership — but **no lead**.
     `householdId` adds the policy to an existing client instead. A submitted
     phone or email that differs from the one on file is not applied; it is
     noted on the welcome call.
  2. **The policy**: `origin: "carrier_direct"`, **no deal**, on the
     household's branch, with the signed application (verified in storage —
     under this row's key, a PDF, ≤ 10 MB), `Active`, its renewal anchor
     derived from the effective date. The carrier is the run's. Nothing is
     credited on performance or the leaderboard, which read deals.
  3. **The hand-off**: the chosen CSR becomes the household's Assigned CRM if
     it has none, and their **welcome call** opens — the onboarding chain's
     first step, "sold by" `Allstate 1-800 (<Bind ID>)`, opening with
     `openingNote` (the prefill's, when omitted).

  The household, the policy and the row's outcome commit together; the
  welcome call opens right after. If it cannot, the answer is still `201`
  with `onboardingId`/`ticketId` `null`, the row waits at `start_onboarding`,
  and `PATCH …/outcome { "kind": "service_intake" }` (the page's Continue)
  opens it — repairing an onboarding written without its call, never
  finishing without one. So do the owner's decision or hand-over of the row,
  and a re-upload of the same period (which carries the outcome to the new
  row either way — still pending, the new row waits on a decision until the
  call opens). A call opened late re-checks its CSR: one no longer an active
  CSR or CRM leaves it unassigned. Only one caller opens it at a time. The ids in the
  answer are what this request created; `row` is the caller's view of the
  row, or `null` if the owner took it back meanwhile. Otherwise the row is
  **done** and resolved `service_intake_recorded` (the owner's review cannot
  pick it).

  Any later report that lists the policy matches it clean (tab Matched,
  context issue `direct_1800`). A **re-upload of the same period** — the run
  it replaces — also carries this outcome, its decision and its assignee to
  the new row, as long as that row asks nothing (a premium Dash and the app
  now disagree on reopens it instead). Next month's report is a new run, so
  its row is simply matched, with no outcome. The policy number has to be
  this Dash line's (400 otherwise).

  ## Body
  - `householdId` — optional, an existing client
  - `primaryContact` — `firstName`, `lastName` (1–60), `dateOfBirth`
    (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `phone` (10–20), `email`
  - `address` — optional `{ street, city, state, zip }`, the living address
  - `members` — ≤ 10 of `{ firstName, lastName, dateOfBirth?, role }`, role
    `Spouse` | `Child` | `Driver` | `Additional Named Insured`
  - `policy` — `policyNumber`, `policyType` (an app policy type), `premium`
    (≥ 0), `itemCount` (≥ 1), `effectiveDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`),
    `newBusinessApplication` `{ key, filename, contentType, size }` from
    `Presign Service Document`
  - `assignedCsrId` — one of `Service Intake Options`
  - `openingNote` — optional, ≤ 2000 characters

  ## Response `201`

  ```json
  { "householdId": "…", "policyId": "…", "onboardingId": "…", "ticketId": "…",
    "row": { "id": "…", "outcome": { "kind": "service_intake", "status": "done", … },
             "review": { "status": "resolved", "resolution": "service_intake_recorded", … }, … } }
  ```

  ## Errors
  - `400` — validation; `RECONCILIATION_OUTCOME_NOT_ALLOWED` — the row is not
    a 1-800 policy the app lacks (a matched one takes Other only); the
    application is not under this row's key or not a PDF; the number fails
    the carrier's format; the CSR is not in the pool
  - `403` `RECONCILIATION_OUTCOME_FORBIDDEN` — no `leads:write`
  - `404` — no such row, or not assigned to the caller; the application never
    reached storage; the pinned household is not one the caller can see
  - `409` — the row is decided, already set up for service, or recorded
    another way (`RECONCILIATION_OUTCOME_LOCKED`); its run was replaced or is
    unfinished; CRM service is off for the agency; the policy number is
    already on a sale in the app (the row is stale — record Other).
    Answers the form can act on, as for a lead: `ambiguous_household` (the
    person belongs to several households — `households[]` lists them; send
    `householdId`) and `contact_deceased` (the client on file has died)
}
